    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "mg_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "MIDI Garden\n\nPlug in a MIDI keyboard or controller: every note you play plants a flower (louder notes, bigger flowers) and plays it. Knobs sending CC 21, 22, 23, 24 turn the garden's Hue, Petals, Spin and Bloom (the filter too) — set other CC numbers on the MidiCC nodes to match your controller. No MIDI? Everything has a stand-in: the four sliders do the knobs, keys A–K play notes, and clicking plants a flower where you click (higher up = higher note).\n\nHow it works: a note-on is a press, or a new note while held, from whichever source is playing. Each one appends the flower's place, time and note to three lists kept by Read* → Write* pairs (the newest 28). A ForEach draws every flower as a rose curve that grows in, turns and slowly wilts (two Envelopes); a knob's CC wins over its slider once it has moved.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
